  "problem": "Exact named-source requests could resolve to unrelated catalog descriptions mentioning similar words. Not-yet-indexed identities could invent catalog membership. Title equality could delete or merge records among the 579 repeated-title cases. An unavailable named source could be fabricated as an exact match. Catalog membership and source-family recognition could be conflated. Editing sealed identity family-graph.mjs or fingerprint-sealed question-parser.mjs would break WP7 / retrieval algorithm fingerprints.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Named-source resolution lives in packages/enrichment/named-sources.mjs with an expanded packages/retrieval/fixtures/named-source-registry.v1.0.0.json covering the core cohort and twelve expansion families. MEPS/HCUP/NPPES/PHC4 exact-name fixtures cannot resolve to unrelated descriptions mentioning similar words. Not-yet-indexed identities do not invent catalog membership. The 579 repeated-title cases are accounted for; title equality alone never deletes or merges a record. Unavailable named sources return a bounded coverage-gap explanation, not a fabricated exact match. Catalog membership and source-family recognition remain distinct. Sealed packages/identity/src/family-graph.mjs (4322 bytes) and fingerprint-sealed packages/retrieval/tools/question-parser.mjs (10068 bytes) are unchanged.",
